+## When `beforeSession` throws
+
+- A `beforeSession` hook that throws fires `onError` with the session and the thrown error — the same `(session, error)` shape as any other orchestrator failure — and the caller still receives that same error as a rejection ([validated by: fires onError with the session and the thrown error, and still rejects the caller with it](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L31)).
+- A `beforeSession` hook that throws still fires `afterSession`, after `onError`, and the caller still receives the thrown error as a rejection ([validated by: fires afterSession after onError, and still rejects the caller with the thrown error](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L48)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
 These three properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
